{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 44, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 18, "tex": "\\section{Introduction}"}, {"line": 19, "tex": "\\label{section-introduction}"}, {"line": 21, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 22, "tex": "In this chapter we do just enough work to construct the Picard scheme"}, {"line": 23, "tex": "of a projective nonsingular curve over an algebraically closed field."}, {"line": 24, "tex": "See \\cite{Kleiman-Picard} for a more thorough discussion as well as"}, {"line": 25, "tex": "historical background."}, {"line": 27, "tex": "\\medskip\\noindent"}, {"line": 28, "tex": "Later in the Stacks project we will discuss Hilbert and Quot functors"}, {"line": 29, "tex": "in much greater generality."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 31, "section_label": "section-introduction", "section_start_line": 18, "section_title": "Introduction", "source_file": "pic.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
{"candidate_ids": ["candidate.stacks.238759b255c3e2adfb57b38d", "candidate.stacks.76ea98f99d3481cb08859759", "candidate.stacks.3e65081947d3a544c0a993af", "candidate.stacks.c8cb6f4f46be341704ff274f", "candidate.stacks.81de3668c7d10e98bdcf87e2", "candidate.stacks.e10193e87caed14651198666"], "chapter_number": 44, "locally_named_context_leads": [{"kind": "remark", "label": "remark-when-proposition-applies", "line": 371}], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 246, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 32, "tex": "\\section{Hilbert scheme of points}"}, {"line": 33, "tex": "\\label{section-hilbert-scheme-points}"}, {"line": 35, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 36, "tex": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $d \\geq 0$ be an integer."}, {"line": 37, "tex": "For a scheme $T$ over $S$ we let"}, {"line": 38, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 39, "tex": "\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}(T) ="}, {"line": 40, "tex": "\\left\\{"}, {"line": 41, "tex": "\\begin{matrix}"}, {"line": 42, "tex": "Z \\subset X_T\\text{ closed subscheme such that }\\\\"}, {"line": 43, "tex": "Z \\to T\\text{ is finite locally free of degree }d"}, {"line": 44, "tex": "\\end{matrix}"}, {"line": 45, "tex": "\\right\\}"}, {"line": 46, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 47, "tex": "If $T' \\to T$ is a morphism of schemes over $S$ and if"}, {"line": 48, "tex": "$Z \\in \\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}(T)$, then the base change"}, {"line": 49, "tex": "$Z_{T'} \\subset X_{T'}$ is an element of $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}(T')$."}, {"line": 50, "tex": "In this way we obtain a functor"}, {"line": 51, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 52, "tex": "\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S} :"}, {"line": 53, "tex": "(\\Sch/S)^{opp} \\longrightarrow \\textit{Sets},\\quad"}, {"line": 54, "tex": "T \\longrightarrow \\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}(T)"}, {"line": 55, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 56, "tex": "In general $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$ is an algebraic space"}, {"line": 57, "tex": "(insert future reference here). In this section we will"}, {"line": 58, "tex": "show that $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$ is representable"}, {"line": 59, "tex": "by a scheme if any finite number of points in a fibre of"}, {"line": 60, "tex": "$X \\to S$ are contained in an affine open."}, {"line": 61, "tex": "If $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$ is representable by a scheme, we often"}, {"line": 62, "tex": "denote this scheme by $\\underline{\\Hilbfunctor}^d_{X/S}$."}, {"line": 64, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 65, "tex": "\\label{lemma-hilb-d-sheaf}"}, {"line": 66, "tex": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. The functor $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$"}, {"line": 67, "tex": "satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology"}, {"line": 68, "tex": "(Topologies, Definition \\ref{topologies-definition-sheaf-property-fpqc})."}, {"line": 69, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 88, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 89, "tex": "\\label{lemma-hilb-d-limit-preserving}"}, {"line": 90, "tex": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $X \\to S$ is"}, {"line": 91, "tex": "of finite presentation, then the functor $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$"}, {"line": 92, "tex": "is limit preserving (Limits, Remark \\ref{limits-remark-limit-preserving})."}, {"line": 93, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 113, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 114, "tex": "Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $i : X \\to Y$ be a closed immersion of schemes"}, {"line": 115, "tex": "over $S$. Then there is a transformation of functors"}, {"line": 116, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 117, "tex": "\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S} \\longrightarrow \\Hilbfunctor^d_{Y/S}"}, {"line": 118, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 119, "tex": "which maps an element $Z \\in \\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}(T)$ to"}, {"line": 120, "tex": "$i_T(Z) \\subset Y_T$ in $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{Y/S}$. Here $i_T : X_T \\to Y_T$"}, {"line": 121, "tex": "is the base change of $i$."}, {"line": 123, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 124, "tex": "\\label{lemma-hilb-d-of-closed}"}, {"line": 125, "tex": "Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $i : X \\to Y$ be a closed immersion of schemes."}, {"line": 126, "tex": "If $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{Y/S}$ is representable by a scheme, so is"}, {"line": 127, "tex": "$\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$ and the corresponding morphism of schemes"}, {"line": 128, "tex": "$\\underline{\\Hilbfunctor}^d_{X/S} \\to \\underline{\\Hilbfunctor}^d_{Y/S}$"}, {"line": 129, "tex": "is a closed immersion."}, {"line": 130, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 163, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 164, "tex": "\\label{lemma-hilb-d-separated}"}, {"line": 165, "tex": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $X \\to S$ is separated and"}, {"line": 166, "tex": "$\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$ is representable,"}, {"line": 167, "tex": "then $\\underline{\\Hilbfunctor}^d_{X/S} \\to S$ is separated."}, {"line": 168, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 193, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 194, "tex": "\\label{lemma-hilb-d-An}"}, {"line": 195, "tex": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of affine schemes. Let $d \\geq 0$. Then"}, {"line": 196, "tex": "$\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$ is representable."}, {"line": 197, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 298, "tex": "\\begin{proposition}"}, {"line": 299, "tex": "\\label{proposition-hilb-d-representable}"}, {"line": 300, "tex": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $d \\geq 0$. Assume"}, {"line": 301, "tex": "for all $(s, x_1, \\ldots, x_d)$ where $s \\in S$ and"}, {"line": 302, "tex": "$x_1, \\ldots, x_d \\in X_s$ there exists an affine open $U \\subset X$"}, {"line": 303, "tex": "with $x_1, \\ldots, x_d \\in U$. Then $\\Hilbfunctor^d_{X/S}$ is"}, {"line": 304, "tex": "representable by a scheme."}, {"line": 305, "tex": "\\end{proposition}"}, {"line": 371, "tex": "\\begin{remark}"}, {"line": 372, "tex": "\\label{remark-when-proposition-applies}"}, {"line": 373, "tex": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. The assumption of"}, {"line": 374, "tex": "Proposition \\ref{proposition-hilb-d-representable} and"}, {"line": 375, "tex": "hence the conclusion holds in each of the following cases:"}, {"line": 376, "tex": "\\begin{enumerate}"}, {"line": 377, "tex": "\\item $X$ is quasi-affine,"}, {"line": 378, "tex": "\\item $f$ is quasi-affine,"}, {"line": 379, "tex": "\\item $f$ is quasi-projective,"}, {"line": 380, "tex": "\\item $f$ is locally projective,"}, {"line": 381, "tex": "\\item there exists an ample invertible sheaf on $X$,"}, {"line": 382, "tex": "\\item there exists an $f$-ample invertible sheaf on $X$, and"}, {"line": 383, "tex": "\\item there exists an $f$-very ample invertible sheaf on $X$."}, {"line": 384, "tex": "\\end{enumerate}"}, {"line": 385, "tex": "Namely, in each of these cases, every finite set of points of"}, {"line": 386, "tex": "a fibre $X_s$ is contained in a quasi-compact open $U$ of $X$"}, {"line": 387, "tex": "which comes with an ample invertible sheaf, is isomorphic"}, {"line": 388, "tex": "to an open of an affine scheme, or is isomorphic to an open"}, {"line": 389, "tex": "of $\\text{Proj}$ of a graded ring (in each case this follows"}, {"line": 390, "tex": "by unwinding the definitions). Thus the existence of suitable"}, {"line": 391, "tex": "affine opens by"}, {"line": 392, "tex": "Properties, Lemma \\ref{properties-lemma-ample-finite-set-in-affine}."}, {"line": 393, "tex": "\\end{remark}"}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 397, "section_label": "section-hilbert-scheme-points", "section_start_line": 32, "section_title": "Hilbert scheme of points", "source_file": "pic.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": [{"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 64, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 64, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 69, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 71, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 88, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 88, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 93, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 95, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 123, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 123, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 130, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 132, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 163, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 163, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 168, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 170, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 193, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 193, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 197, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 199, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "proposition", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 298, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["proposition"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 298, "scope_stack": ["proposition"]}, {"environment": "proposition", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 305, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["proposition"]}, {"kind": "pro